{{Quote|But I was going into Tosche Station to pick up some power converters!"<br />"You can waste time with your friends when your chores are done.|Luke Skywalker and Owen Lars|audio=ToscheStation.flac|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
'''Tosche Station''' was a power station and repair shop on the outskirts of [[Anchorhead]] on the [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Tatooine]], owned by [[Merl Tosche]] and operated by [[Laze Loneozner]].<ref name="Complete Locations" /> During the time of the [[Galactic Civil War]], Loneozner was friends with [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Biggs Darklighter]], who, prior to becoming a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], spent [[time]] at the station with Lonezner, his girlfriend [[Camie Marstrap]], and other youth from Anchorhead.<ref name="Episode IV" /> After witnessing a [[Secret mission to Tatooine|battle]] between the Rebel Alliance and the [[Galactic Empire]] in the skies over Tatooine, Skywalker told his friends about what he had seen, but they did not believe it had been a battle. It was at Tosche Station that Darklighter informed Skywalker that he was defecting from the Empire to join the Rebel Alliance.<ref name="Biggs Databank">{{Databank|biggs-darklighter|Biggs Darklighter}}</ref>

==Layout==
[[File:ITW_Tosche_Station.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Station cutaway]]
A [[Power Station|power station]] and repair shop, Tosche Station was located just outside of the city of Anchorhead on the [[Great Chott salt flat]] of Tatooine. The station was owned by Merl Tosche but he seldom visited, instead allowing his employee Laze "Fixer" Loneozner to run the shop.<ref name="Complete Locations" />

The station consisted of three buildings; the main building housed recharge facilities, a sales office, and game room. Next to the main building was a spare parts garage and repair shop. Behind the main building was the reactor building, which held a [[fusion generator]] from an in-system [[space barge]]. The reactor generated energy which was transmitted via underground power conduits to buildings in Anchorhead as well as nearby [[moisture farm]]s.<ref name="Complete Locations" />

==History==
Merl Tosche owned Tosche station, but rarely visited. Customers appeared infrequently, giving Loneozner free rein of the station. Loneozner spent most of his time at the station with his friends, including his girlfriend Camie Marstrap, Luke Skywalker, Biggs Darklighter, [[Windy]], and [[Deak]]. Loneozner secretly worked on building a [[podracer]] in the spare parts garage, which he intended to sell at [[Mos Espa]], using the profits to fund his wedding to Camie.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> Tosche Station was Skywalker's favorite place to hang around with his friends at.<ref name="World Building">{{InsiderCite|227|World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)}}</ref> 

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> Skywalker went to the station to tell his friends about a battle he saw raging between two ships high above Tatooine. It was at this time that Biggs Darklighter informed Skywalker that he intended to abandon his newly assigned post on the Imperial [[starship]] ''[[Rand Ecliptic]]'' and join the Rebel Alliance.<ref name="Episode IV" /><ref name="Complete Locations" /> After the [[Battle of Yavin]], Skywalker reminisced he never picked up the [[power converter]]s he mentioned before he left Tatooine.<ref name="Heir to the Jedi">''[[Heir to the Jedi]]''</ref>

[[File:Anchorhead-BoBF.png|thumb|right|250px|Boba Fett arrives to the station.]]
After the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], former [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]] tracked a gang of [[Nikto]]&mdash;the [[Kintan Striders Gang|Kintan Striders]] [[Kintan Strider speeder bike|speeder bike]] gang&mdash;to Tosche Station, where they were harassing Loneozner and Camie. Fett entered the establishment and quickly dispatched the gang, later stealing their [[speeder bike]]s to bring back to the Tusken tribe in preparation for their assault on a [[Pyke Syndicate]] [[hovertrain]].<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Tosche Station was originally going to appear in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], but was cut from the film. The scene was, however, released in the deleted scenes of the special features of the Blu-Ray release of the [[original trilogy]]. The scene shows Luke Skywalker telling his friends about a space battle he saw above the planet.

The location and layout of the station were made canon, as well as the station's owner, Merl Tosche, when it was included in the 2016 version of [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']].

Scenes at Tosche Station were filmed at the Sidi Jemour Mosque on [[Djerba]] island, [[Tunisia]].<ref name="Star Wars Kids (1997) 14">[[Star Wars Kids (1997) 14|''Star Wars Kids'' (1997) 14]]</ref>

